        "layout": "#########\n#PL..G###\n#.#..####\n#.##C@G##\n#......##\n#########",
        "design_notes": "Human-feedback and critic-driven revision of L05 v3. The opening ordinary crate pull is compressed to one high-responsibility move: it opens the route into the upper P/L corridor and prepositions the same crate beside the lower target. The P/L anchor is then handled in the middle of the route, first by a right pull from the L side and then by two right pushes from the P side. This three-step boundary shift makes the previously prepositioned crate finishable from the left, so the final ordinary-crate push recovers the opening move instead of acting as a stitched add-on. Complete graph analysis reports a 24-step shortest solution over 85 reachable states. Direction-aware event probe is complete with no winning bypass missing anchor_pull_right, anchor_push_right, crate_pull, or crate_push; anchor shift count probe is complete with no win below three P/L boundary shifts. Independent evidence review returned pass, and independent puzzle critic returned accept. Caveat: the level is strongly guided and the second consecutive P/L right push is more reinforcement than a new insight, but that is acceptable for the fifth curriculum slot. Pending human playtest; not archived yet.\n",
